  "term": "backward conditioning",
  "definition": "Backward conditioning is a conditioning arrangement in which the unconditional stimulus is presented before the conditional stimulus. In the supplied study, this US-then-CS order did not produce conditioning, unlike the CS-then-US sequence.",
